  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(0.9)=25.841\\,932{\u2026}^{\u2218}\u2248{25.84}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${25.84}^{\u2218}$ lies inside the required domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={25.84}^{\u2218}.$\n\nOur first solution lies in the first quadrant and has a reference angle of \n${\\theta }_{R}={25.84}^{\u2218}.$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the fourth quadrant, and it also has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}={25.84}^{\u2218}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13978101/assets/4c65ecb4fdcefc332b75f2b459f65ba872a2d2d0826b27ba80df1c8f8f3b606e.png)\n\nA second solution $X$ lies in the $4$th quadrant, and we can find it using the reference angle, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={360}^{\u2218}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={360}^{\u2218}-{25.84}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={334.16}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, this value is not in the required domain. To get a second solution that's within the required domain, we simply subtract ${360}^{\u2218}$ from $X:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =X-{360}^{\u2218} \\\\  & ={334.16}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218} \\\\  & =-{25.84}^{\u2218}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=25.84\\cdot (-25.84)\u2248-670\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest ten.",
